{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","name":"CSI Crime Scene and Biohazard Cleanup Questions","url":"https://answers.cleansceneinvestigators.com/answers/","publisher":{"@id":"https://www.cleansceneinvestigators.com/#organization"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Who cleans up after police leave a crime scene?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"After law enforcement releases the property, cleanup is generally arranged separately by the owner, family, landlord, property manager or another authorized representative. A specialty remediation company handles the physical cleanup."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do police clean crime scenes?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Police and Crime Scene Investigators investigate and process the scene. They generally do not perform post-release biological remediation of the property."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who cleans after an unattended death?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"After the appropriate authority releases the scene, a professional trauma or biohazard remediation company can handle the physical cleanup of blood, bodily fluids, decomposition contamination and affected materials."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a funeral home clean the house after someone dies?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Typically no. Funeral homes care for and transport the deceased. Structural biohazard cleanup is a separate service."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can decomposition odor be removed?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often yes. Effective odor remediation begins by identifying and addressing the source and affected materials before treating residual odor."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can blood soak through flooring?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Depending on the amount, time and flooring system, fluids can migrate through seams, carpet, padding, underlayment or into subflooring."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does insurance cover biohazard cleanup?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Some property policies may cover part of specialty cleanup depending on the event, policy terms, exclusions, limits and carrier decision."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does biohazard cleanup cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Cost depends on the size of the affected area, contamination depth, materials, labor, disposal, odor treatment, access and restoration needs. A reliable estimate should be tied to a defined scope."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a vehicle be restored after a biohazard incident?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sometimes. Salvageability depends on where contamination traveled, the materials and components affected, access, duration and the overall condition of the vehicle."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where does CSI: Clean Scene Investigators serve?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"CSI is based in North Texas with Denton, Denton County and Dallas-Fort Worth as its home market, and provides statewide Texas response for qualifying specialty cleanup calls."}}]}